xoneration) — rejected: limb (b) requires that the driver did not reply within 120 seconds of the rider's locating message, and he replied at 22:50:05, 30 seconds after her 22:49:35 message, so the clause does not apply and the content of the reply is irrelevant to it; the rider's refund does not depend on this clause, because it follows from POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06. (6) POL-NS-07 — the anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations in 30 days, 2/93 = 0.02, both below the thresholds), so there is no escalation on that ground; no driver compensation is payable because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 provides a payout on these facts. (7) The driver's statement that he 'arrived and waited' is not accepted: it is contradicted by his own telemetry across the whole window and is corroborated by no admissible fix. Amount and confidence: the refund is the cancellation-fee line only — EV-FARE-02710 shows cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The deciding fact (the driver's position) is carried by EV-GPS-02710 at weight 1.00 and by the trip record at 1.00, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.00; I set confidence at 0.95. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger applies: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, POL-NS-05 resolves the conflict between the arrival marker and the trace, the anti-farming check does not trip, and no impaired artifact carries the deciding fact. Two claims that cited the missing advisory (EV-ADVIS-02710-01) were discarded by the referee for not naming its issue code and are listed in the audit record. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes automatically, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
