    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02710, weight 1.0 — 64 fixes at 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps) never places the vehicle inside the 150 m arrival radius for this TRANSPORT_HUB pickup: the derived arrival block reports 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 seconds. His closest approach to the pin (Bedok Interchange PHV bay) over the whole trace is 517.4 m, his mean distance is 1,618.8 m, and his speeds run to 63.0 km/h. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02710, weight 1.0) carries a driver-pressed arrival marker (arrival_marker BUTTON) at 22:48:55 and a driver cancellation at 22:53:55 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW.\n\nWhy the fee falls. POL-NS-02: there is no qualifying in-radius fix at any point in the 15 minutes before cancellation, so the driver is not deemed to have arrived and POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. The wrong-entrance arguments run by both advocates under POL-NS-03 fail on arithmetic — that clause's ceiling is 400 m from the pin and the driver's closest fix is 517.4 m, so this is not a wrong face of the same venue but a driver who was never at the pickup; POL-NS-03 does not govern. POL-NS-05: the 'arrived' marker at 22:48:55 is false, because the trace places the vehicle far beyond 300 m from the pin and in motion at 28.8–63.0 km/h, so the waiting clock cannot run from it; with no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip, limb (ii) refunds the fee in full with no compensation and records the false-arrival event. POL-NS-06 reaches the same result independently: effective in-geofence dwell 0.0 s against the 180 s free waiting period in force for this trip, a 180 s shortfall. Accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable because the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02710-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), and the shortfall therefore stands unexcused.\n\nThe rider-exoneration claims. POL-NS-04 is argued by both sides but does not apply. Limb (a) is met — the rider's message at 22:49:35 ('where are you? i dont see any car') is a locating message. Limb (b) is not met: the driver replied at 22:50:05, 30 seconds later and well inside the 120-second window, and POL-NS-04 expressly does not apply where the driver replied within 120 seconds, whatever the reply says. The rider-presence evidence (54 of 54 rider fixes qualifying, mean 5.4 m and maximum 8.6 m from the pin, stationary) is accepted as fact but does not change the outcome: the fee falls on the driver's position, not the rider's, and limb (c) alone decides nothing.\n\nThe driver's side. The counterparty statement ('I arrived and waited, the rider did not come') carries no weight multiplier and is directly contradicted by the driver's own trace; it is not accepted. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full, POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displace it, and POL-NS-07 therefore does not engage. The anti-farming check does not trip on either advocate's figures (no_show_terminations_30d 2, below the count of 4; 2/93 = 0.0215, below the rate of 0.08) — but that is not the reason compensation fails; the failure of POL-NS-01 limb (b) is. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires: POL-NS-05 resolves the only apparent conflict (arrival marker against trace), so limb (b) is not engaged; there is no anti-farming trip and no repeat-dispute pattern (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0); and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The POL-NS-03(ii) pin-ambiguity goodwill does not arise, because it requires stationary fixes within 400 m of the pin and there are none.\n\nMoney and effect. The fare ledger EV-FARE-02710 (weight 1.0) shows the cancellation-fee line at SGD 4.50, total charged SGD 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00; that line, and only that line, is refunded. The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so 